findings.body:
**A TS repo that later gains a Python manifest (and has no vulture) refuses every `pup audit` until someone re-runs `pup init`.**

`isNewGap` only checks whether the previous capture's `gaps` record holds the pair. It doesn't check whether the previous capture ran that adapter at all:

```ts
function isNewGap(previous: ProjectBaseline, gap: DebtGap): boolean {
  if (previous.gaps === undefined) return false;
  return !previous.gaps.some(
    (g) => g.adapterId === gap.adapterId && g.capability === gap.capability,
  );
}
```

How it plays out:
- A TS-only repo stores `{ adapters: ['typescript'], gaps: [] }`.
- The repo later gains a `pyproject.toml` or a `requirements.txt`. `pythonAdapter.detect` turns on from the manifest alone (`src/adapters/python.adapter.ts` L25, L249-251). The CLI runs `auditProject` with the adapters it detects now, `detectAdapters(repoPath)` (`src/cli/index.ts` L1920), not the stored list.
- With no vulture declared, `deadCode` returns `unavailable` (python.adapter.ts L293-294). `measureDebt` then records the gap `('python', 'dead code')`.
- `previous.gaps` is `[]`, so the gap counts as new. `persistBaseline` is skipped, so `gaps` never learns about the Python gap. The merge-gate ratchet (`src/core/merge-gate.service.ts` L1132-1138) carries the old `gaps` forward too. Every plain audit and every `--sweep` exits 1 with "Baseline kept".
- Nothing is protected. The stored `deadExports` only ever held the TS share, which is the case this function's docstring says must not block. The refusal tells the operator to "fix the measurement and re-run `pup audit`" and never mentions `pup init`, which is the only way out short of installing vulture.

Coverage doesn't hit this with the built-in adapters. `measureDebt` takes coverage from the first adapter that offers it, so a newly detected adapter that takes over coverage would really drop `coverageRatio`. The guard below is therefore limited to dead code. A test that inits with `[ts]` and audits with `[ts, pyWithout]` would pin this down.

https://github.com/AlexisBalayre/pupitre/blob/3ccfa1b9b99615550ab75afe88efb21580b3190b/src/core/audit.service.ts#L129-L134

findings.suggestion:
function isNewGap(previous: ProjectBaseline, gap: DebtGap): boolean {
  if (previous.gaps === undefined) return false;
  // An adapter the stored capture did not run added no share to its flat deadExports.
  if (gap.capability === 'dead code' && !previous.adapters.includes(gap.adapterId)) return false;
  return !previous.gaps.some(
    (g) => g.adapterId === gap.adapterId && g.capability === gap.capability,
  );
}
